# Who reviews a change to this handbook.
#
# Ownership lives here rather than in a per-page `owner:` frontmatter field on
# 52 pages. Two reasons: with the department at its current size every page
# resolves to the same person, so the field would be 52 copies of one fact; and
# a frontmatter owner is a claim nothing enforces, while this file routes the
# review request on GitHub. When the team grows past one reviewer, sections get
# their own lines here — the page still says nothing, and the routing stays
# true. See /about/team.mdx for the roles behind these handles.
#
# Last matching pattern wins, so keep the catch-all first.

*                           @seifsameh14

# Build, deploy and verification machinery — a change here can ship a broken
# page with a green build, which is exactly what the checks exist to prevent.
